      "writtenOn": "2021-10-25T06:40:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "board_get_default_battery_type()  gets called only in the case where (type\u003d\u003d  BATTERY_TYPE_COUNT) , which means manufacturer name read from fuel guage doesnt match that of  board_battery_info.\nReference : common/battery_fuel_gauge.c : 93\nFor example, as in getac type battery, where manufacturer name is same, irrespective of 2s/3S cell type, call to board_get_battery_cell_type will not be hit only, as name matches.\n\nAlso, Currently, i see only a single driver ln9310\n(driver/ln9310.c:434: batt \u003d board_get_battery_cell_type();) \n that  uses board_get_battery_cell_type() , which decides 2S or 3S type battery  and follows different initialization based on it.",
      "parentUuid": "5891a82c_d10e76a7",
      "revId": "cff0d5838faa4cf32e95340060316d096ea0672d",
